G. Coordination with CAISO 
Horizon West also clarifies in Section 8.1.5.1 that energization is conditioned on the 
Eligible Customer demonstrating that:  

• The Interconnection Agreement and Cost Recovery Agreement are effective;  
• Any Energy the Large Load withdraws from the CAISO Controlled Grid will be 
purchased from an entity authorized to make such sales by the applicable Local 
Regulatory Authority;  
• A Scheduling Coordinator will represent the Large Load in compliance with Section 
25.7.3 or 25.7.3.1 of the CAISO Tariff;  
• Access Charges will be paid consistent with the CAISO Tariff;  
• The information required by Section 25.7.1 of the CAISO Tariff has been provided; 
• Required equipment to facilitate monitoring, disturbance recording, telemetry, 
communication, control, protection, and disconnection has been installed, tested, and 
commissioned;  
• Any FILI Service Agreement is effective;  
• All required financial security has been posted;  
• For co-located or behind-the-meter configurations, control and protection technologies 
have been validated, and the Large Load is separately metered.  This ensures no Large 
Load is energized until the information and equipment necessary to preserve reliability 
and to operate consistent with CAISO requirements is in place; and 
• The Large Load meet all frequency ride-through requirements, voltage ride through 
requirements, post-fault active power recovery requirements, and ramp rate limitations in 
accordance with CAISO Tariff Sections 25.7.1.1, 25.7.1.2, 25.7.1.3, and 25.7.1.4.  
H. Ministerial and Conforming Revisions 
Horizon West has also made several ministerial or conforming revisions to either clarify 
or correct its tariff language or to better clarify the Horizon West Tariff’s relation to the CAISO 
Tariff.  These include: 
• Updating the Table of Contents; 
• Clarifying in Section 1 that Horizon West does not provide retail electric service; 
• Clarifying in Section 1.3 how End-Users access the CAISO Controlled Grid; 
• Defining FILI Service in Section 3.35 consistent with the CAISO Tariff; 
• Clarifying Gross Load’s definition in Section 3.40 to better match CAISO; 
• Revising the definition of “Interconnection” in Section 3.41 to address a typographical 
error; 
• Defining Interconnection Facilities in Section 3.44 to provide clarity; 

